## UI vocabulary

| Never say | Say instead |
|-----------|-------------|
| Ledger | **Hisaab** |
| Customer / Supplier | **Party** |
| Inventory tab | **Items** / **Maal** |
| Sale Invoice | **Sale** / **Bikri** |
| Purchase Invoice | **Purchase** / **Kharid** |
| Credit | **Udhaar** |
| Payment received | **Jama** / **Paisa mila** |
| Payment paid | **Paisa diya** |
| Expense | **Kharch** |
| Receivable / Payable | **Lena Hai** / **Dena Hai** |
| Stock, Inventory, SKU, Barcode | **Never show in UI** |

## Item Master (Maal — shortcuts only)
**Purpose:** speed up Bikri/Kharid — **not inventory**.

Each item: **Item Name** + **Unit** (required) · **Purchase Rate** + **Sale Rate** (optional defaults on master form only).

**Inline create** from Sale/Purchase: name + unit only — auto-create, no detour.

**List:** name + unit only. **Never** show quantity, alerts, barcode, SKU, or warehouse.

**Internal compatibility:** legacy DB columns may exist — never expose in UI or product docs. On edit, preserve existing internal data without surfacing it.

**Never add** to Item Master without project owner approval: GST %, HSN, brand, description, images, barcode, SKU, weight, or other inventory/business-management fields.

**Phase C 🔒 FROZEN (docs only):** optional GST **entry helper** spec in `PROJECT_RULES.md` — **do not implement** (no code, UI, DB, routes, calculations, migrations) until production gates pass: real-world testing → bug fixes → performance → production APK → user feedback → proven daily stability. Default OFF · manual GST % · GST Extra / GST Included · transaction-only · not GST accounting.

## Development priority (permanent — do not skip)
```
Phase A ✅  →  Phase B ✅  →  Real-world Testing  →  Bug Fixes  →  Performance  →  Production APK  →  User Feedback  →  Phase C (optional, frozen)
```
Workflow fixes from user feedback **beat** new features. Phase C never delays bug fixing or production readiness.

## Item creation (inline — 2 fields)
**Item Name** + **Unit** only — a shortcut for faster entry, **not inventory**.

## Party creation (up to 3 fields)
**Name** (required) · **Mobile** (optional) · **Previous Balance** (optional). One Party for buyer and seller.

## Entry forms
- **Jama / Paisa diya:** Party, Amount, Date, Note (optional)
- **Kharch:** Expense name, Amount, Date, Note (optional)
- **Sale / Purchase:** Party, Date, payment mode, line items (qty + rate) — register style, not invoice

Pick or instant-create Party and Item inline. No master-data detours.

## Navigation (5 tabs)
Dashboard · Hisaab · Items · Sale · Purchase — no separate Customer/Supplier tab.

## Automatic (hidden from user)
Hisaab balances, dashboard totals, and history update when entries are saved. **No inventory/stock UX** — ever, unless project owner explicitly approves.
No invoice printing, PDF bills, or e-way.

## Scale
Stay fast at 100,000+ transactions. Paginate lists; index `date`, `party_id`, `type`, name search.

## Out of scope
Inventory/stock management (Section 12), Tally-style accounting UI, GST return filing, tax invoices, HSN screens, item codes, stock groups — unless project owner revises rules in `PROJECT_RULES.md`.

